---
// The about page: what the site is and how facts are labelled.
import '../../styles/trust.css';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, isRealUrl } from '../../lib/site';

const contactUrl = isRealUrl(SITE.contactUrl) ? SITE.contactUrl : null;
---

<Base title="About" current="about">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Independent by design.</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="sec prose trust">
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      Exposure Focus is part of <a href="https://www.infosecuriosity.co.uk/" rel="noopener">infosecuriosity</a>, developed by Stephen Tate.
      It cuts through the hype around new vulnerabilities and gives real, actionable intelligence on exposure,
      so you can make informed decisions about how urgent each one is for your setup and what to do about it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every verdict follows a published rubric, so you can see <a href="/rubric/">how we decide</a>.
      There are no sponsors, affiliate links, advertising, tracking or third-party scripts.
    </p>

    <h2>How facts are labelled</h2>
    <p>Every fact has a source link and an as-of date. Each carries one of three labels:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Vendor-stated:</strong> the maker of the product said it.</li>
      <li><strong>Reported:</strong> someone credible reported it, and we have not confirmed it ourselves.</li>
      <li><strong>Inference:</strong> our own reasoning from the facts above.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Claims we have not confirmed are labelled as such, never stated as fact. Every call can change as the evidence does, and the date on each verdict shows when it was last checked. Mistakes are listed on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.</p>

    {contactUrl && (
      <>
        <h2>How to contact us</h2>
        <p><a href={contactUrl} rel="noopener">Contact the author</a></p>
      </>
    )}

    <h2>Verdicts are guidance, not a guarantee</h2>
    <p>A verdict is our reading of the evidence on the date shown. It does not know your systems, so check the evidence date before you act.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
